  englishName: Dongpo Pork
  chineseName: 东坡肉
  pinyinName: Dongpo Rou
  category: 1
  difficulty: 1
  briefDescription: Braised pork belly named after the famous poet Su Dongpo.
  detailedDescription: A famous Hangzhou dish made by pan-frying and then red cooking pork belly. The pork is cut into a square, consisting of half fat and half lean meat.
  historicalOrigin: Attributed to Su Dongpo in the Song Dynasty.
  culturalSymbolism: Symbolizes the refined literary culture of Jiangnan.
  regionalSignificance: A classic of Hangzhou/Suzhou cuisine.
  craftmanshipNotes: Requires long braising time for tenderness.
  estimatedDuration: 300
